1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lucius Caecilius Metellus Denter was consul in 284 BC, and praetor the year after. In this capacity he fell in the war against the Senones, and was succeeded by Manius Curius Dentatus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fischer, in his ''Römische Zeittafeln'', has him as praetor and also dying in 285 BC, and in the year following he has him again as consul. Drumann denies the identity of the consul and the praetor, on the ground that it was not c
2 CONC ustomary for a person to hold the praetorship the year after his consulship; but examples of such a mode of proceeding do occur, so Drumann's objection fails.
2 CONT
2 CONT Denter may have been the father of Lucius Caecilius Metellus, consul in 251 and 247 BC. The latter's filiation is given as "L. f. C. n.", the son of Lucius and grandson of Gaius. In this case, Denter's father would have been Gaius
2 CONC  Caecilius Metellus. An alternative hypothesis makes him the son or nephew of a Quintus Caecilius, supposedly tribune of the plebs in 316 BC. No corresponding individual appears in ''The Magistrates of the Roman Republic'', or in 
2 CONC the ''Dictionary of Greek and Roman Biography and Mythology''.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucius Julius Libo was a member of the influential Julii clan. This patrician family was always of the most distinguished blood, however they had long since fallen out of the inner Roman elite. The Julii were active in politics si
2 CONC nce the Punic Wars.
2 CONT
2 CONT Libo descended from the Julii who fled from Alba Longa to Rome. This city was destroyed by the Roman king Tullus Hostilius. His ancestors claimed their descent from the goddess Venus and the first Roman king Romulus. He had a son 
2 CONC of the same name Lucius Julius Libo II with Caecilia Metella Macedonica, daughter of Lucius Caecilius Metellus Denter and '''Barsine of Macedonia.'''   
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucius_Caecilius_Metellus_Denter Lucius Caecilius Metellus Denter]
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucius_Julius_Libo Lucius Julius Libo]
