2 CONT =Marcus Cocceius Anicius Faustus Flavianus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcus Cocceius Anicius Faustus Flavianus (fl. 3rd century AD) was a Roman senator who was appointed suffect consul sometime around AD 250/252.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably either the son or nephew of Anicius Faustus Paulinus, suffect consul before AD 230, Faustus Flavianus was a member of the Patrician 3rd century gens Anicia. Faustus Flavianus was appointed Curator rei publicae Cirtae (or 
2 CONC curator of the city of Cirta) in AD 251. It is believed that sometime around this time, c. AD 250/252, he was appointed suffect consul.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is speculated that Faustus Flavianus was the brother of Sextus Cocceius Anicius Faustus Paulinus, suffect consul prior to AD 268.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Cocceius_Anicius_Faustus_Flavianus
