1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Anicius Probinus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Anicius Probinus (fl 395-397) was a politician and aristocrat of the Roman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT A member of the noble gens Anicia, Probinus was the son of Sextus Claudius Petronius Probus, one of the most influential men of his era and consul in 371, and of Anicia Faltonia Proba; he was then the brother of Anicius Hermogenia
2 CONC nus Olybrius, Anicius Petronius Probus and Anicia Proba. According to a reconstruction, Probinus was the father of Petronius Maximus, briefly Western Roman emperor in the spring of 455.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probinus was raised with his brother Olybrius in Rome, where he was born. He divided with his brother the consulate in the year 395, while both were very young; on this occasion to the two brothers was dedicated a panegyric by Cla
2 CONC udian (Panegyricus de consulatu Probini et Olybrii). Although they originated in a family belonging to the Roman senatorial aristocracy, traditionally pagan, Olybrius and Probinus were Christians; the appointment as consuls of the
2 CONC se two Christians may have been a signal, desired by the emperor Theodosius I, the very next year to the usurpation and Pagan restoration of Eugenius.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probinus was then proconsul of Africa in 396-397.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT With his brother he received the dedication of the work Exempla elocutionum by Arusianus Messius, and both received a letter (Epistles, v) by Quintus Aurelius Symmachus in 397. It is known that he composed verses.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anicius_Probinus
