1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Prince Mirian or Miri (Georgian: მირიანი; მირი) was a Georgian prince of royal Chosroid dynasty reigning between 736 and 741.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was son of Prince Stephen of Kakheti and brother of Prince Archil of Kakheti. According to the chronicle his father divided between his two sons the royal treasure of silver and gold jewels before taking refuge to Colchis (West
2 CONC ern Georgia). The second half of the royal treasury was left to his second son, the future ruler Archil of Kakheti "the Martyr", who remained in Kakheti. The reign of Mirian was brief. He was seriously injured in a fight against t
2 CONC he Arab forces, he died, leaving the throne to his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mirian had 7 daughters. Future husbands for his daughters had been assigned by his brother Archil. Names of most of the princesses are not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT anonymous daughter, wife of Guaram IV of Iberia
2 CONT
2 CONT anonymous daughter, wife of Pitiakhsh (Arshusha VI?), a descendant of Peroz, Duke of Trialeti
2 CONT
2 CONT anonymous daughter, wife of Nersianid Prince Nerse I Nersiani. They had son Adarnase III of Iberia.
2 CONT
2 CONT anonymous daughter, wife of Adarnase Adarnasiani
2 CONT
2 CONT anonymous daughter, wife of Duke Varazman
2 CONT
2 CONT anonymous daughter, wife of Juansher Juansheriani
2 CONT
2 CONT Gurandukht, wife of Leon I of Abkhazia
