1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_of_Ibelin_(died_1304)_
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/JERUSALEM%20NOBILITY.htm#GuyIbelinJaffadied1304<br/>
2 CONT 4.         GUY Ibelin ([1250/55]-14 Feb 1304, bur Nicosia Cemetery).  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "Jaque, Johan et Gui" as the three sons of "Johan conte de Japhe & his wife"[578].  Another manuscript of the Lignages c
2 CONC onfirms that "Guiotin" was son of "Johan…conte de Japhe"[579].  Titular Count of Jaffa.  The Chronicle of Amadi records the death 14 Feb, in 1304 from the context, of "Guido de Iblim, conte de Zaplio" and his burial "al semiterio 
2 CONC de Nicosia"[580].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[m''' firstly ---.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.  However, Guy´s estimated birth date, and the date of his marriage to his known wife, suggest the likelihood of an earlier marriage
2 CONC .''']'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [secondly] ([1290]) MARIE Ibelin Lady of Ascalon and Naumachia, daughter of PHILIPPE Ibelin & his wife Simone de Montbéliard (-after 1324).  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "Marie, Aalis, Helvis, Eschive et Marguer
2 CONC ite" as the five daughters of Philippe Ibelin & his wife, stating that Marie married "Gui, le conte de Japhe"[581].  The Chronicle of Amadi names "Maria de Iblim, sorella de messer Balliam principe de Gallilea et signor de Thabari
2 CONC e" as wife of "messer Guido de Iblim conte de Zapho, chiamato Piscopia"[582].  The Chronicle of Amadi records that "la contessa del Zapho et de Ascalona et dama de Rames, madama Maria de Iblim" and "le sue doe sorelle…madama Alisa
2 CONC  moglie di messer Galtier de Bessan, dama de Colletta, et madama Eschiva, dama di S. Nicolò, moglie de messer Galtier Dampiere" were "retained at the royal court…and imprisoned in the house of the Lord of Tyre"[583].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy Ibelin & his second wife had five children:  
