2 CONT b. 12 January 1276 or 11 January 1277.
2 CONT Isabella of Armenia was Princess/Lady of Tyre. She was a daughter of Leo II of Armenia and his wife, Keran. (She was also their third daughter to be named Isabella (both previous daughters had died in early childhood). She was the
2 CONC  twin sister of Sempad. In 1293 in Nicosia she married Amalric of Cyprus, by whom she had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh
2 CONT Henry (died c. 1323)
2 CONT Guy (died 1344)
2 CONT John (died 1343)
2 CONT Bohemond (died 1344)
2 CONT Maria, who married her cousin Leo IV of Armenia
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella, along with her son Henry, were imprisoned and murdered by Oshin of Corycos. Oshin, who was acting as regent for Leo IV of Armenia, wanted to reduce the number of claimants to the throne of the Cilician Kingdom.
