1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_of_Ibelin_(1286%E2%80%931308)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Guy of Ibelin''' (1286–1308), Lord of Nicosia,[1] was the son of Balian of Ibelin, seneschal of the kingdom of Cyprus, and of Alice of Lampron.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1303, with papal dispensation, he married his cousin Isabella of Ibelin,[2] daughter of Baldwin of Ibelin and of Marguerite de Giblet. Their only child was Alix of Ibelin, second wife of Hugh IV of Cyprus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy was buried on September 8, 1308 in the Premonstratensian Abbey of Bellapais near Kyrenia, Cyprus.[3]
