2 CONT i)          '''BALIAN''' (-killed in battle near Botrun 1277).  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Balian, Johan et Marguerite" as the three children of "Julien…sire de Saiete" and his wife "Femie, la fille au roi Heiton d'Ermenie"[100
2 CONC 4].  He succeeded his father as titular Lord of Sidon.  He was killed in battle fighting with Bohémond Count of Tripoli against Guy II Embriaco of Jebail[1005].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' MARIE of Jebail, daughter of HENRI Embriaco Lord of Jebail & his wife Isabelle Ibelin (-before 22 Jan 1290).  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Marie, la fille au seignor de Giblet" as the wife of "Balian" son of "Julien…sire 
2 CONC de Saiete"[1006].  Balian & his wife had two children (who were legitimated per dispensationem post matrimonium contractum 23 May 1289, on the basis that their parents' marriage had been contracted without the necessary Papal disp
2 CONC ensation despite being related in the 4th degree[1007]): 
2 CONT
2 CONT *(a)       EUPHEME .  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "Femie et Ysabeau" as the children of "Balian", son of "Julien…sire de Saiete", & his wife, stating that Euphemie married "Heiton, le fis dou mareschal d'Ermenie et ore
2 CONC nt ii fis et une fille"[1008].  1290.  <br>  '''m''' HETHUM [V] of Lampron Lord of Simangla, son of OSHIN [IV] Lord of Asgouras and Marnick & his wife Agatha --- ([1265]-1307). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *(b)       ISABELLE .  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "Femie et Ysabeau" as the children of "Balian", son of "Julien…sire de Saiete", & his wife, stating that Isabelle married "Mansel de Buillon et orent une fille"[1009].
2 CONC   1290.   <br>   '''  m''' MAURICE de Bouillon
