2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CYPRUS.htm#AliceIbelinM1HuguesIVCyprusM2
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          ALIX Ibelin ([1304/06]-after 6 Aug 1386, bur Dominican Church).  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Aalis" as the daughter of Guy Ibelin & his wife[746].  The Chronicle of Amadi records the marriage 17 Sep, in 1317 or 1318 
2 CONC from the context, of "messer Hugo de Lusignan contestabile del regno de Cypro, nepote del…re" and "Alisia de Iblim, figlia de messer Guido, signor del castello de Nicosia"[747].  The dispensation issued by Pope John XXII for the m
2 CONC arriage of "Hugues de Lusignan connest. regis Cyprie nepos Henrici regis, viduus Mariæ" and "Alice Ibelin filia quondam Guidonis" is dated 18 Jun 1318[748].  The dispensation issued by Pope Urban V for the marriage of "Philippe de
2 CONC  Brunswick dux viduus Alisiæ de Dampierre" and "Alice Ibelin vidua Hugonis regis" is dated 29 May 1368[749].  [750]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' (1310) to HENRI de Lusignan, son of AMAURY of Cyprus Lord of Tyre & his wife Zabel of Armenia (-murdered in Armenia [1322/9 Apr 1323]).  After the family of Amaury was exiled to Armenia, this betrothal was terminat
2 CONC ed.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (Papal dispensation 18 Jun 1318) as his second wife, HUGUES of Cyprus, son of GUY of Cyprus, Constable of Cyprus & his wife Eschiva Ibelin (-10 Oct 1359).  Constable of Jerusalem 1318-1324.  He succeeded in 1324 as
