2 CONT '''Irene Palaiologina ''' (Greek: Εἰρήνη Παλαιολογίνα; 1327 – after 1356) was a Byzantine princess and Bulgarian empress consort.[1] She was also known as '''Maria Palaiologina ''' (Μαρία Παλαιολογίνα).
2 CONT
2 CONT Her parents were Andronikos III Palaiologos and Anna of Savoy, whilst her siblings were John V Palaiologos[2] and Michael Palaiologos.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married in 1336 Tsar Michael Asen IV of Bulgaria. In 1355, her husband was killed in battle with the Ottoman Turks near Sofia. Irene decide to stay a nun in the monastery in Mesembria (today Nesebar) and take the name Matiasa.
2 CONC  She died around 1399 and was buried in Mesembria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nothing else is known about her, except that she was an Orthodox Christian.
