1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantine_II_of_Georgia
2 CONT
2 CONT Constantine II (Georgian: კონსტანტინე II) (c. 1447 – 1505), of the Bagrationi dynasty, was a king of Georgia since 1478. Early in the 1490s, he had to recognise the independence of his rival rulers of Imereti and Kakheti, and to c
2 CONC onfine his power to Kartli.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1503, due to the expansion of neighbouring Safavid Iran, the Kingdoms of Kartli and Kakheti became Safavid vassals. In 1505, Constantine II died, and was succeeded by his son David X.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://nobility.pro/genealogy/individual.php?pid=I6726&ged=tree
