1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/VENICE.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT        MARCO Cornaro ([Venice 1435/43]-).  Patrician of Venice.  m FIORENZA Crispo, daughter of NICCOLÒ Crispo Lord of Santorin and Syra & his wife [Valenza] --- ([Venice 1435/43]-).  Marco & his wife had eight children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a.       VIOLANTE .  m MARCO Dandolo, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b.         CATERINA Cornaro (Venice [30 Apr/25 Nov] 1454-Venice 10 Jul 1510).  The life of Caterina Cornaro by Antonio Colbertaldi d'Asolo records her birth in 1454 to "Firenze, figliola di Nicolò Crespi duca di Arcipelago, e da M
2 CONC arco Corner nobile Veneto" and her death at Venice 10 Jul 1510, clarifying that she was her father's second daughter[276].  A document dated 1468 records the betrothal of "la fia de Marco Corner kavalier…Catherina" and "el re Zacc
2 CONC o" at Venice, also naming "Andrea Corner…fradello de Marco Corner"[277].  On her marriage, she was adopted by the Venetian state under the name 'Caterina Veneta'.  Famed for her beauty, she was painted many times, including by Tit
2 CONC ian.  She was declared regent of Cyprus by Venice, her adoptive 'parent', on the death of her husband, continuing as such after the birth of her son.  Venice permitted her to succeed her son 1474 as CATERINA Queen of Cyprus, Jerus
2 CONC alem and Armenia, but was forbidden to remarry or exercise any real power.  She was finally obliged to abdicate as Queen 24 Jun 1489 in favour of the Republic of Venice[278], the Cornaro family receiving in recompense the heredita
2 CONC ry Grand Commandership in Cyprus of the Order of St John and the right to quarter their arms with those of Lusignan[279].  She left Cyprus for Venice, where she was made Signora di Asolo.  m (by proxy Venice 10 Jun 1468, in person
2 CONC  Famagusta Dec 1472) JACQUES II King of Cyprus, illegitimate son of JEAN II King of Cyprus & his mistress Marieta --- ([1438/39 Famagusta 11 Jun 1473). 
2 CONT
2 CONT c.         CORNELIA .  m PAOLO Vendramino, son of ANDREA Vendramino Doge of Venice & his wife ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT d.         REGINA [Elisabetta] .  m (1478) PAOLO Capello, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT e.         GIORGIO Cornaro ([Venice 1450/63]-1524).  A Venetian document dated 28 Oct 1488 records the Council decision that Caterina Cornaro should leave Cyprus and that "vir nobilis Georgois Cornario, frater prefate…regine" shou
2 CONC ld travel to Cyprus to effect her departure[280].  m ---.  Descendants. 
2 CONT
2 CONT f.          BIANCA .  m PIETRO Lando, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT g.         '''AGNESE .  m NICOLO Querini''', son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT h.         daughter .  m --- Querini, son of ---. 
