2 CONT Like his father, he followed a military career. He was registered in the regiment of the host of René de Belleval, in the division of the Count of Alençon, for the war against England. He also served with his company of 10 men in 
2 CONC the region of Poitou
2 CONT
2 CONT participated in the siege	2  SOUR S20
2 CONT 	3  PAGE p. 13
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT in the Battle||fighting against the troops of the Black Prince
2 CONT
2 CONT took part in the battles of Ploërmel and of Honfleur under the command of the marshal of Normandy, Robert de Clermont	2  SOUR S20
2 CONT 	3  PAGE p. 13
2 CONT 	2  SOUR S140
2 CONT 	3  PAGE fol. 42
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT is referred to as Jean I in The Canarian and in the Nobiliário da Ilha da Madeira which incorrectly indicates his father as Regnault de Bethencourt, but then includes information from 1346-1357, including his marriage to Isabeau d
2 CONC e St. Martin	2  SOUR S22
2 CONT 	3  PAGE p. xliii
2 CONT 	2  SOUR S140
2 CONT 	3  PAGE fol. 41v-42
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Familias Faialenses lists Jean (II)'s father as Renaud de Béthencourt, and Renaud's father as Filipe de Béthencourt. However, it also states that Jean (II) died in 1357 in the Battle of Honfleur and that Filipe lived in the time o
2 CONC f Louis VIII of France. Louis VIII lived 1187-1226, reigned 1223-1226. It is highly improbable that Filipe's grandson, Jean (II), could have died over 125 years later. There must be more generations in between. Therefore I have ch
2 CONC osen to follow the line of descent as given in Os Bettencourt
