1 OCCU Карл IV де Бурбон, херцог на Вендом, Duc de  Vendãome, Duke of Vendome 1514-1537, Duc de Vendôme, etc, Duke of Vendôme; AKA "Charles de Bourbon", Duke of Vendôme
1 TITL Duke
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Charles de Bourbon (2 June 1489 – 25 March 1537) was a French prince du sang and military commander at the court of Francis I of France.'''
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT '''Charles was born at the Château de Vendôme, eldest son''' of Francis de Bourbon, Count of Vendôme and Marie of Luxembourg.[1][2]
2 CONT '''Charles succeeded his father as Count of Vendôme in 1495. Charles's first military service was in Italy, under King Louis XII of France. In 1514, he was created Duke of Vendôme when the county of Vendôme was elevated into a duc
2 CONC hy.[3] He fought at the Battle of Marignano (1515)[4] and participated in the Flemishb campaign. Because of his loyalty to the King, he was appointed head of the council when King Francis I was captured at the Battle of Pavia.'''[
2 CONC 5]
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT '''On 18 May 1513, Charles married Françoise d'Alençon''',[6] eldest daughter of René, Duke of Alençon[7] and Margaret of Lorraine. '''They had:'''
2 CONT 1. Louis de Bourbon (1514–1516), died in infancy.
2 CONT 2. Marie de Bourbon (1515–1538), unmarried, prospective bride of King James V of Scotland in 1536.
2 CONT 3. Marguerite de Bourbon (1516–1559), married in 1538, Francis I, Duke of Nevers (1516–1561)[7]
2 CONT 4. Antoine de Bourbon, Duke of Vendôme (1518–1562),[2] King of Navarre through his marriage (jure uxoris) in 1548 to Queen Jeanne III.
2 CONT 5. François de Bourbon, Count of Enghien (1519–1546), unmarried.
2 CONT 6. Madeleine de Bourbon (1521–1561), Abbess of Sainte-Croix de Poitiers.
2 CONT 7. Louis de Bourbon (1522–1525), died in infancy.
2 CONT 8. Charles de Bourbon (1523–1590), Archbishop of Rouen[8]
2 CONT 9. Catherine de Bourbon (1525–1594), Abbess of Soissons.
2 CONT 10. Renée de Bourbon (1527–1583), Abbess of Chelles.
2 CONT 11. Jean de Bourbon, Count of Soissons and Enghien (1528–1557), married in 1557, his first cousin, Marie, Duchess of Estouteville (1539–1601)[8]
2 CONT 12. Louis I de Bourbon, Prince of Condé (1530–1569),[9] married in 1551 with Eléonore de Roye, daughter of Charles de Roye, Count of Royce then in 1565 with Francoise d'Orléans-Longueville.
2 CONT 13. Léonore de Bourbon (1532–1611), Abbess of Fontevraud.
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles%2C_Duke_of_Vend%C3%B4me
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Sir Charles IV de Bourbon, Duke of Vendome, Count of Soissons, Marle, Conversano'''1
2 CONT Last Edited	20 Mar 2002
2 CONT M, #18346, '''b. 2 June 1489, d. 25 March 1537'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	François de Bourbon, 4th Count & 1st Duke de Vendome b. 1470, d. 2 Oct 1495
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Marie of Luxembourg d. 1 Apr 1547
2 CONT '''     Sir Charles IV de Bourbon, Duke of Vendome, Count of Soissons, Marle, Conversano was born on 2 June 1489 at Vendome, France. He married Francoise d' Alencon''', daughter of Rene, 3rd Duke d'Alencon, Comte de Perche, Vicomt
2 CONC e de Beaumont and Margareta of Lorraine, '''on 18 May 1513 at Chateaudun, France. Sir Charles IV de Bourbon, Duke of Vendome, Count of Soissons, Marle, Conversano died on 25 March 1537 at Amiens, France, at age 47.'''
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT '''Francoise d' Alencon''' b. c 1491, d. 14 Sep 1550
2 CONT '''Children'''	
2 CONT *Louis de Bourbon, Comte de Marle2 b. 23 Sep 1514, d. 7 Apr 1516
2 CONT *Marie de Bourbon2 b. 29 Oct 1515, d. 28 Sep 1538
2 CONT *Marguerite de Bourbon+ b. 26 Oct 1516, d. 20 Oct 1589
2 CONT *Antoine de Bourbon, 2nd Duke of Vendome, King of Navarre+ b. 22 Apr 1518, d. 17 Nov 1562
2 CONT *Francois de Bourbon, Comte d'Enghien, Governor of Hennegau2 b. 23 Sep 1519, d. 23 Feb 1546
2 CONT *Madeleine de Bourbon2 b. 3 Feb 1521, d. a 18 Nov 1561
2 CONT *Louis de Bourbon2 b. 3 May 1522, d. 25 Jun 1525
2 CONT *Charles de Bourbon, Bishop of Nevers, Archbishop of Rouen, Papal Legate2 b. 22 Dec 1523, d. 9 May 1590
2 CONT *Catherine de Bourbon2 b. 18 Sep 1525, d. 27 Apr 1594
2 CONT *Renee de Bourbon2 b. 6 Feb 1527, d. 9 Feb 1583
2 CONT *Jean III, 3rd Comte de Soissons, 5th Duke d'Estouteville b. 16 Jul 1528, d. 10 Aug 1557
2 CONT *Louis I de Bourbon, Prince of Conde+ b. 7 May 1530, d. 13 Mar 1569
2 CONT *Eleanore de Bourbon2 b. 18 Jan 1532, d. 26 Mar 1611
