1 OCCU Duchess Consort of Guise, Fondatrice de l'hôpital Sainte-Croix de Joinville
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Antoinette of Bourbon, Duchess of Guise (25 December 1494 – 22 January 1583), was a French noblewoman of the House of Bourbon. She was the wife of Claude of Lorraine, Duke of Guise.'''
2 CONT Life
2 CONT '''Antoinette de Bourbon was born on 25 December 1494 at the Chateau de Ham, in the Somme department, Picardy, France. She was the child of''' Francis, Count of Vendôme and Marie de Luxembourg.[1][2] '''Her paternal grandparents w
2 CONC ere''' John VIII, Count of Vendôme and Isabelle de Beauvau, '''and her maternal grandparents''' were Peter II, Count of Saint-Pol, and Margaret of Savoy.
2 CONT '''Antoinette was described as having been a remarkable woman, combining a strong sense of family pride with a wry sense of humour. She exhibited considerable administrative talent at domestic economy as well as in the running of 
2 CONC the vast Guise dominions surrounding their chateau of Joinville.'''
2 CONT '''Antoinette exerted a powerful influence on the childhood of her granddaughter''' Mary, Queen of Scots, during the latter's thirteen-year sojourn in France, and '''was one of her principal advisors. Antoinette acted as proxy for
2 CONC  her daughter,''' Mary of Guise, '''during the betrothal ceremony of the Queen of Scots and the Dauphin Francis on 19 April 1558.'''[3]
2 CONT '''Antoinette and her family have been described as "ultra-Catholic"; in 1533 Antoinette oversaw the burning of a Protestant man caught preaching in the town of Wassy.[4] Her son''' Francis, Duke of Guise was held to be responsibl
2 CONC e for the anti-Protestant Massacre of Wassy on 1 March 1562 which was one of the early atrocities in the French Wars of Religion.[5]
2 CONT '''Antoinette de Bourbon died on 22 January 1583 at the Chateau de Joinville. She was eighty-eight years of age, having outlived all of her children except her daughter''' Renée, Abbess of St. Pierre.
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT '''Antoinette married Claude of Lorraine on 9 June 1513;[6] they had:'''
2 CONT *Mary of Guise (1515–1560); married first Louis II, Duke of Longueville,;[7] secondly King James V of Scotland in 1538. Their daughter was Mary, Queen of Scots.[8]
2 CONT *Francis, Duke of Guise (1519–1563)[6]
2 CONT *Louise of Guise (10 January 1520 – 18 October 1542); married Charles I, Duke of Arschot on 20 February 1541.
2 CONT *Renée of Guise (2 September 1522 – 3 April 1602), Abbess of St. Pierre, Reims. She was the only one of Antoinette's many children to outlive her mother.
2 CONT *Charles of Guise (1524–1574), Duke of Chevreuse, Archbishop of Reims, and Charles, Cardinal de Guise.[6]
2 CONT *Claude, Duke of Aumale (1526–1573)[6]
2 CONT *Louis, Cardinal de Guise (1527–1578)[6]
2 CONT *Philip of Guise (3 September 1529 – 24 September 1529, Joinville)
2 CONT *Peter of Guise (3 April 1530); died young.
2 CONT *Antoinette of Guise (31 August 1531 – 6 March 1561), Abbess of Faremoutiers
2 CONT *François de Lorraine, Grand Prior (18 April 1534 – 6 March 1563)[9]
2 CONT *René II de Lorraine, Marquis d'Elbeuf (1536–1566)[6]
2 CONT Etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antoinette_of_Bourbon
2 CONT ______
2 CONT '''Antoinette de Bourbon'''1
2 CONT Last Edited	7 Dec 2008
2 CONT F, #18007, '''b. 25 December 1493, d. 22 January 1583'''
2 CONT '''Father'''	François de Bourbon, 4th Count & 1st Duke de Vendome b. 1470, d. 2 Oct 1495
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Marie of Luxembourg d. 1 Apr 1547
2 CONT Charts	
2 CONT 14 Generation Pedigree of George III, King of Great Britain & Ireland
2 CONT 14 Generation Pedigree of Friedrich Wilhelm III, King of Prussia
2 CONT '''     Antoinette de Bourbon was born on 25 December 1493 at Ham. She married Claude I de Lorraine, Duke d'Aumale, Comte de Guise''', son of Renatus II, Duke of Lorraine & Bar, Count Vaudemont, d'Harcourt, & Guise, Baron de Joinv
2 CONC ille, King of Sicily & Jerusalem and Philippa of Guelders, '''on 9 June 1513 at Paris, France. Antoinette de Bourbon died on 22 January 1583 at Chateau de Longueville, France, at age 89.'''
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT '''Claude I de Lorraine, Duke d'Aumale, Comte de Guise''' b. 20 Oct 1496, d. 12 Apr 1550
2 CONT '''Children	'''
