1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Voir [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suzanne_de_Bourbon '''Wikipedia...''']
2 CONT * From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Suzanne de Bourbon-BeaujeuSuzanne de Bourbon, suo jure Duchess of Bourbon (10 May 1491– 28 April 1521, Château de Châtellerault) was Duchess of Bourbon and Auvergne from 1503 to her death.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter and only surviving offspring of Peter II of Bourbon and Anne of France, daughter of King Louis XI of France. She became duchess regnant in 1503 after the death of her father. Her mother became her regent durin
2 CONC g her minority and negotiated for several different marriages to ensure that she was given a spouse which would protect her position.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 10 May 1505, at Château du Parc-les-Moulins, Suzanne married her cousin Charles of Bourbon-Montpensier, head of the Montpensier family, a cadet branch of the Bourbons. Her husband was made her co-regent through marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Suzanne of Bourbon had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis, Count of Clermont. He was born on July 17, 1517, and died c.January or February 1518. 
2 CONT
2 CONT An unnamed pair of twins. They were born dead, Suzanne having suffered either a miscarriage or a still-birth in the wake of Francis' death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband kept his position as duke of Bourbon after her death. Her death witouth heirs caused Her lands eventually to become a part of France.
